WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:12.100
Pasteur settled a real question: grape juice sealed from the air stayed inert, while

2
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.820
juice open to airborne yeast foamed into alcohol.

3
00:00:15.733 --> 00:00:21.113
Fermentation was biology: it appeared only alongside living, multiplying yeast.

4
00:00:22.013 --> 00:00:27.133
Pasteur invoked no vital force; his was an empirical claim, and a stronger one than

5
00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:31.693
his data required: that fermentation could not be separated from the living cell.

6
00:00:32.483 --> 00:00:37.343
From the very man who proved fermentation was alive, that conviction hardened into a

7
00:00:37.343 --> 00:00:41.783
40-year orthodoxy, and it would take a flask of dead yeast to dissolve it.
